<div class="exercise"><div class="ex-q"><p>Why give collision shapes that differ from the visual meshes?</p>
</div><details><summary>Show the solution</summary><div class="ex-s"><p>Collision checking runs many times per planning step or simulation step. Simple primitives (boxes, cylinders, capsules) or convex hulls are much faster and more robust than detailed meshes, while the visual mesh only needs to look right.</p>
</div></details></div>
